{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
In [G]South Australia I was [D]born,
[G]Heave away! [D]Haul away!
In [G]South Australia round Cape [C]Horn,
We're [D]bound for South Aus[G]tralia.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Haul away, you rolling [D]king,
[G]Heave away! [D]Haul away!
[G]Haul away, you'll hear me [C]sing,
We're [D]bound for South Aus[G]tralia.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
As [G]I walked out one morning [D]fair,
[G]Heave away! [D]Haul away!
'Twas [G]there I met Miss Nancy [C]Blair,
We're [D]bound for South Aus[G]tralia.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
There [G]ain't but one thing grieves my [D]mind,
[G]Heave away! [D]Haul away!
To [G]leave Miss Nancy Blair be[C]hind,
We're [D]bound for South Aus[G]tralia.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
